From 03d185a003ad9c9e6da7c2e706b2264a75128898 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FerFemNemBem <74377239+FerFemNemBem@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:17:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] camellia: leave out liboemcrypto (Widevine L3)

Without liboemcrypto.so the Widevine HAL cannot reach the TEE and falls back to
software security level L3. Workaround for the broken MediaTek secure video path
(protected playback fails with the source-built kernel): DRM apps then use the
normal video decoder and play in SD resolution. Optional, see WIDEVINE_L3.
---
 proprietary-files.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/proprietary-files.txt b/proprietary-files.txt
index a508b9a..6751841 100644
--- a/proprietary-files.txt
+++ b/proprietary-files.txt
@@ -1027,7 +1027,7 @@ vendor/firmware/nt36672d_tm_03_ts_mp.bin
 vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.drm@1.4-service.widevine
 vendor/etc/init/android.hardware.drm@1.4-service.widevine.rc
 vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/manifest_android.hardware.drm@1.4-service.widevine.xml
-vendor/lib64/liboemcrypto.so
+# vendor/lib64/liboemcrypto.so  (left out on purpose: Widevine falls back to L3, see crdroid-camellia-builder WIDEVINE_L3)
 vendor/lib64/libtlcWidevineModularDrm.so
 vendor/lib64/liburee_meta_drmkeyinstall.so
 vendor/lib64/libwvhidl.so
-- 
2.43.0

